{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it. A client macro that requires ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Step"},{"text":" stores ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"any Step.Type"},{"text":"; until there is one (or in tests","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that use a kind of their own), mark a static let typed as the existential metatype:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["protocol Step: SendableMetatype {","    static var name: String { get }","}","","struct First: Step { static let name = \"first\" }","","enum Steps {","    @LinkerSetEntry(kind: .steps)","    static let first: any Step.Type = First.self","}","","let steps = LinkerSet<any Step.Type>(kind: .steps).values"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Step"},{"text":" refines ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SendableMetatype"},{"text":" because a static let must be ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"text":" in Swift 6, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"any Step.Type"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"text":" only when the protocol says its metatypes are. Without it the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"compiler warns that the property isn’t concurrency-safe (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MutableGlobalVariable"},{"text":"), which is an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"error in a build that treats warnings as errors. A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@MainActor"},{"text":" protocol, such as a UIKit delegate","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"protocol, refines it the same way.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Order","anchor":"Order","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Records come back image by image in the order the loader lists them (the program, then its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":